   Headless (zero-interaction) battery design case under the **virtual-battery-factory** skill protocol, workspace `D:\research\degradation_prognostics\Battery_Design_Agent\runs\exp\t2_r1_noceiling`. Task text (verbatim contract): "Design a battery for grid energy storage: energy density ≥ 327.18 Wh/kg, support 4C fast charge (no lithium plating), anode SEI thickness ≤ 500 nm after 100 cycles of 1C cycling, discharge capacity retention ≥ 90% at -20°C, SEI ≤ 550 nm after 500 cycles. Ablation note: ceiling_escalation switch OFF — do not proactively escalate into material design; use materials/systems named in the task text only, otherwise tune within the existing cell/architecture formulation space."
   
   Zero-interaction rules: no clarification questions; parse parameters from task text; use defaults for unspecified; write thresholds + degree-of-freedom parsing to log.jsonl entry 0; threshold values verbatim from task text; all conclusion-grade values from tool outputs only; all evaluations via `bda log-evaluate` (mechanical verdict); **every propose round must have a same-round evaluate** (verify-deliverables prerequisite); real_compute defaults false; deliverable closing required (design_spec.md, bom.xlsx, datasheet.md, calc.xlsx, dvpr.md, dfmea.md, delivery_index.md + PDF releases flat in deliverables/, render report.html, verify-deliverables PASS, endorse/final entries).

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - Virtual Battery Factory 5-stage funnel (plan→materials→cell→safety→true DFT/MD); start_stage=3 (cell design) since no materials named; evaluation-and-fallback control loop
   - Ablation switches: ceiling_escalation OFF (task text), exploration_force ON (2–4 variants/round), funnel_voting ON (moot)
   - Decision criteria in `inputs/entry0.json`: stage2 energy_density_wh_kg min 327.18, sei_100cyc_nm max 500, sei_500cyc_nm max 550, lowT_retention min 0.9; stage3 plated false; meta.freedoms: electrode_system locked, electrolyte_formulation adjustable, electrode_modification locked, cell_architecture adjustable, thermal_management adjustable
   - PyBaMM Chen2020 SPMe; plating module ("irreversible", j0 0.001 A/m², defaults injected); SEI "ec reaction limited"; aging = [discharge 1C to v_min, charge 1C to v_max] × cycles, isothermal
   - **PyBaMM "Discharge capacity [A.h]" per cycle is the NET integral (discharge − charge)** — cycle-1 "1.648 Ah" = 4.94 − 3.29 Ah; the capacity climb over cycles is an artifact of the charge step shortening as SEI resistance grows (cli-commands.md also documents this: "climb-then-saturate artifact (lithium loss shifts the voltage window) — annotate honestly")
   - **4C plating mechanism (diagnosed this session)**: the 4C charge aborts at V=4.2 in ~33 s (cathode particle surface diffusion limit, D_s_pos = 4e-15); at the abort the anode representative-particle surface stoichiometry has rocketed to ~0.8 (surface OCP 0.092 V) while the bulk is at ~0.06 (bulk OCP 0.4955 V); metric = "Negative electrode surface potential difference at separator interface" = φ_s − φ_e (delta_phi = phi_s − phi_e in PyBaMM composite surface form, solved via C_dl differential equation); η_neg(sep) ≈ −0.1485 V; electrolyte potential collapses ~0.8 V across the separator during charge; the metric is pinned by the abort race → single levers net out small (B worse −0.4494, C +0.002, D +0.032)
   - Aging protocol temperature verified: aging runs used `aging_1C_100cyc` (25°C/298.15 K) — byte-identical reproduction (sei 449.116, cap1 1.64795, cap100 2.18464)
   - Honest C-rate bookkeeping: nominal capacity = measured 1C capacity (D precedent 3.5681 Ah; E/G/H now ~5.744 Ah → 4C = 22.98 A)
   - calc-energy contract formula: ED = ∫V·I_1C dt / Σ(layer thickness×(1−porosity)×density×area); I_1C = Nominal×1; electrolyte excluded (electrolyte_included: false)
   - PowerShell restrictions: no `$()`, no Set-Location, no `&`; use `;` and `if ($?)`; cwd = repo root; venv python = `.venv\Scripts\python.exe`

